1
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:09,720
In a puzzle app, you must move a tile into a slot.

2
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:14,660
You may only reflect, rotate or translate it, maybe more than once.

3
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:16,740
Does the tile ever change size?

4
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:22,090
Pause the video and choose: no, it stays congruent, or yes.

5
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:22,300
No.

6
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:27,270
Reflections, rotations and translations never change the size or shape.

7
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,430
The image is congruent.

8
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:32,380
Remember: a reflection needs a mirror line.

9
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:35,940
A rotation needs an angle, a direction and a centre.

10
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:38,480
A translation needs a vector.

11
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:44,840
To combine transformations, do the first one, then apply the second one to the image.

12
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:48,760
Triangle A has corners 1, 1, then 3, 1, and 1, 4.

13
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:55,800
Reflect it in the Y axis to get B: negative 1, 1, then negative 3, 1, and negative 1, 4.

14
00:00:55,850 --> 00:01:00,510
Then rotate B 180 degrees about the origin to get C.

15
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,200
Your turn.

16
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:03,900
Where does A's corner 3, 1 end up in C?

17
00:01:03,950 --> 00:01:07,170
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:09,480
B's corner is negative 3, 1.

19
00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:14,640
A 180 degree rotation changes both signs: 3, negative 1.

20
00:01:14,690 --> 00:01:18,960
C is 1, negative 1, then 3, negative 1, and 1, negative 4.

21
00:01:19,010 --> 00:01:21,860
That is just A reflected in the X axis.

22
00:01:21,910 --> 00:01:25,310
One transformation does the job of two.

23
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:30,660
Two reflections in perpendicular lines make a 180 degree rotation.

24
00:01:30,710 --> 00:01:31,390
Your turn.

25
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:37,190
Two reflections in parallel lines make: a translation, or a 90 degree rotation?

26
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,840
Pause and choose.

27
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:40,830
A translation.

28
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:46,160
Reflect in X equals 1, then in X equals 4: everything moves 6 to the right.

29
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:49,560
That is twice the gap between the lines.

30
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:50,940
Here is the method.

31
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:54,110
Step 1: do the first transformation.

32
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:57,450
Step 2: apply the second to the image.

33
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:01,410
Step 3: compare the final image with the start.

34
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:05,460
Step 4: describe a single transformation fully.

35
00:02:05,510 --> 00:02:09,410
Translate by 2, negative 1, then by negative 5, 4.

36
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:11,860
Add the vectors: negative 3, 3.

37
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:13,670
One translation.

38
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:17,780
1, 2 goes to negative 2, 1, and 3, 0 goes to 0, 3.

39
00:02:17,830 --> 00:02:23,590
That is a rotation of 90 degrees anticlockwise about the origin.

40
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:24,740
Order can matter.

41
00:02:24,790 --> 00:02:30,130
Doing the same two moves the other way round may give a different image.

42
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:35,400
Describe the single transformation that moves X, Y to X plus 4, Y minus 2.

43
00:02:35,450 --> 00:02:36,250
Ben answers.

44
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:38,230
Which line is wrong?

45
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,890
Line 1 is not complete.

46
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:42,690
A translation needs its vector.

47
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,420
A translation by the vector 4, negative 2.

48
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:54,920
Game engines and robot arms combine rotations and translations many times every second, to move objects into place.

49
00:02:54,970 --> 00:02:56,200
One last question.

50
00:02:56,250 --> 00:03:02,320
Images after reflections, rotations and translations are always: congruent, or bigger?

51
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:05,640
Pause the video and choose.

52
00:03:05,690 --> 00:03:06,350
Congruent.

53
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:08,460
Same size, same shape.

54
00:03:08,510 --> 00:03:13,060
To remember: apply the second transformation to the image.

55
00:03:13,110 --> 00:03:16,090
Two transformations can equal one.

56
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:17,960
Order can matter.

57
00:03:18,010 --> 00:03:20,510
The images stay congruent.

58
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:25,870
Great work! Now practise lesson 13.3 on Camday.
